.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1258 AM PDT Sat Sep 5 2026
(Sunday through next Friday)

Forecast daytime highs Sunday will be similar to Saturday`s highs,
60s/70s coastside/bayside to the upper 70s to lower 80s inland. Dry
weather will continue Sunday. A weakening or break in mid to upper
level troughing will begin on Labor Day with thermal ridging developing
aloft resulting in a warming trend across the forecast area. This will
result in daytime highs warming back to and slightly above normal e.g.
80s to lower 90s inland to far inland locations.

Global models are still showing redevelopment of 500 mb troughing
over the eastern Pacific during the middle of next week. 00z
guidance however is showing some retrogression of the upper level
trough. This will be at the same time remnant tropical moisture
moves northward and may get entrained into the trough. Our official
forecast shows light rain next week, and it still bears monitoring
however the precipitation forecast over our area has trended drier.

