.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 426 AM PDT Sat Sep 5 2026

Patchy stratus is developing along the SF Bay shoreline while fog
is developing across the North Bay Valleys. Not anticipating
stratus/fog to spread beyond the already impacted airports (STS,
APC, HAF, potentially OAK and SFO). Stratus/fog should dissipate
by late morning (approx. 17/18Z) with VFR persisting through the
remainder of the day. Expecting gustier onshore winds to prevail
again today with the SFO-WMC gradient peaking around +9 mb this
afternoon/evening. Occasional gusts to between 20 to 25 knots are
possible at SFO and SJC this afternoon/evening before winds ease
tonight. The marine layer struggles to redevelop again tonight
which will keep stratus patchier again tonight and see a late
stratus return. Stratus redevelopment becomes more likely closer
to 12Z tomorrow (end of TAF period) but more likely will fall
after 12Z (into the next TAF period).

Vicinity of SFO...Patchy stratus is filling in over the SF Bay and
reaching towards SFO. Guidance indicates some potential for patchy
stratus to fill in over SFO this morning but confidence is mixed
as to if clouds will stay scattered or if a ceiling will develop.
If a ceiling develops it will likely be between 12Z to 16Z. Gusty
onshore winds return this afternoon/evening with gusts to around
25 knots possible. Winds decrease overnight with some potential
for stratus to reach SFO after 12Z tomorrow morning.

SFO Bridge Approach...Generally similar to SFO. Satellite shows
stratus developing over the SF Bay within the SFO Bridge Approach
region. CIGs are likely on the IFR-MVFR border with SFO reporting
scattered clouds at 1100 feet. Stratus will clear by late this
morning with some potential for stratus to redevelop early
tomorrow morning.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR expected through late tonight. Breezy
onshore winds develop during the afternoon/evening before winds
ease overnight. Low to moderate confidence that stratus will
redevelop early tomorrow morning given the fact that the marine
layer is struggling to redevelop this weekend. Stratus becomes
more likely closer to 12Z/into the end of the next TAF period.

