.BEACHES...
Issued at 1010 PM PDT Wed Sep 2 2026

A Beach Hazards Statement is in effect Friday-Monday as the swell
from both Hurricane Marie and Hurricane Karina reaches the coast.
As these hurricane whip up the ocean, the waves travel over 1,000
miles in all directions, gradually flattening out to low
amplitude, but long period swell. These waves aren`t very
intimidating if you`re on a boat in the open ocean, but the long
period allows them to push much farther up the beach. Long period
swell always increases the chance for sneaker waves, but that`s
particularly true this weekend since there are 2 different sets of
southerly swell, and their energy will periodically combine. In
addition to sneaker waves, expect strong rip currents and
breaking waves up to 10 ft. As this is a holiday weekend and the
weather is otherwise pretty nice, the exposure to the risk is
high. Avoid the water if you`re not an expert swimmer. If caught
in a rip current, swim parallel to shore until you stop feeling
the pull. Even on the beach, be prepared for sneaker waves this
weekend and never turn your back on the ocean.

